{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"agent_message","text":"Fixed in `index.js:126`.\n\n**Root cause**\n`slugifyWithCounter()` tracked how many times each normalized slug was seen, but it never checked whether the string it actually returned had already been handed out. The `numberless > 2` heuristic only guessed at collisions, so sequences like `slugify('foo')`, `slugify('foo')`, `slugify('foo-2')` produced `foo`, `foo-2`, `foo-2` — a duplicate.\n\n**Fix**\n- Added a `used` set that records every emitted slug (case-insensitively).\n- The plain slug is only returned when it's the slug's first occurrence, the base slug hasn't already spawned counters, and the plain slug is still free.\n- Otherwise it appends a numeric counter, incrementing past any value already emitted, guaranteeing every returned slug is distinct.\n- `reset()` now clears `used` alongside `occurrences`.\n\nThe existing `counter` test expectations are preserved exactly (e.g. `foo-11` still yields `foo-11-1`), all 24 tests pass including the ReDoS guard, and an exhaustive search over 162,302 calls across colliding inputs found zero duplicates."}}
